# Modern Flutter Development Rules

You are a senior Flutter engineer and mobile UI/UX designer.

Build production-quality Flutter applications with a modern,
clean, premium, user-friendly native mobile experience.

## UI / UX

- Use Material 3 as the foundation.
- Create custom UI rather than relying on default Material widgets.
- Prioritize visual hierarchy and usability.
- Keep screens clean and uncluttered.
- Use generous but consistent spacing.
- Use rounded corners consistently.
- Use subtle shadows only when needed.
- Avoid excessive gradients.
- Avoid excessive glassmorphism.
- Avoid unnecessary decorative elements.
- Do not make the UI look like a generic AI-generated template.

## Responsive Design

The application must work across:

- Small Android phones
- Moto G96
- Large Android phones
- Different aspect ratios
- Different screen densities
- Landscape where appropriate

Never design using fixed screen dimensions.

Prefer:

- MediaQuery
- LayoutBuilder
- SafeArea
- Flexible
- Expanded
- Slivers
- SingleChildScrollView

Avoid hardcoded screen heights and widths.

## Design System

Never scatter colors and dimensions throughout widgets.

Create centralized design tokens:

- AppColors
- AppTypography
- AppSpacing
- AppRadius
- AppShadows

Example:

```dart
AppColors.primary
AppColors.background
AppColors.textPrimary

AppSpacing.sm
AppSpacing.md
AppSpacing.lg

AppRadius.md
AppRadius.lg